# Covers: a program parked in `waituntil` is QUIESCENT and is not live
#         work, in BOTH spellings -- `waituntil (cond)` parks on a
#         watcher's wait list, `waituntil (e?)` parks on an event's, and
#         spec section 8 says wait lists do not count.  An armed `at` is
#         the thing that does count, because a host slot write between two
#         steps is what it exists to notice.
# matrix-row: scheduler-quiescence
#
# The two predicates answer different questions and a host must not
# confuse them: `urbi_step` says "is there anything to run right now",
# `urbi_has_live_work` says "is there anything left at all".  An armed
# watcher makes the second true forever while the first stays QUIESCENT,
# which is why an event loop keys its sleep on the step result.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var x = 0
## host: live-work
## host: run waituntil (x == 1)
## host: step 100000
## host: live-work
## host: run var e = Event.new()
## host: run var t = Tag.new()
## host: run t: { waituntil(e?) }
## host: step 100000
## host: live-work
## host: run at (x == 7) { x = 0 }
## host: step 100000
## host: live-work
[00000000] 0
[00000000] live-work: false
[00000000] nil
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] live-work: false
[00000000] <event>
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] live-work: false
[00000000] nil
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] live-work: true
